+## K2c Coordinate Change
+
+The stage engine computes in the declared `K2c` basis:
+
+```text
+K2c_r_q = [t^r(w-1)^q](K3^3 + (t^22 C2)K3 + t^33 C3),
+```
+
+for low `q`, after the major h2 D2 structural state.  The charged structural
+certificate states that the unit leader is `C3c_r_q` for `q<=10` and
+`C2c_r_(q-11)` for `11<=q<=21`.
+
+This gate reconstructs and serializes the inverse as a compact triangular
+ledger:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52gate-20260903/k2c-c2c3-inverse.json
+SHA-256 88e717d691f6ab35336e3a0a387463f4c319d5917c37c417a54f8a2dddf9a768
+```
+
+The ledger has 495 inverse rules, one for each original low-q `C2c/C3c`
+coordinate:
+
+```text
+C2c variables                         187
+C3c variables                         308
+low-q nonidentity output slots         495
+D2 fixed low-q slots                   389
+D2 identity slots outside low-q        (1,22), (1,23), (2,22)
+K2c coordinates before h2-D1           106
+K2c coordinates after h2-D1             99
+inverse_rules_sha256
+aabd8ce03875fcab6432b27f0af8151a2e796ff717d646b8c66af4cb58f37495
+```
+
+The inverse is compact, not fully expanded.  Each rule has diagonal
+coefficient `1` and every nonleader `C2c` dependency is solved earlier in the
+`(r,-q)` order.  The seven h2-D1 eliminations are also recorded:
+
+```text
+K2c_11_16, K2c_15_13, K2c_19_10, K2c_23_7, K2c_27_4,
+K2c_10_17, K2c_14_14
+```
+
+with coefficients
+
+```text
+1, -3, 9, -27, 81, 1, -3.
+```
+
+This is enough for the stage-8 conclusion.  A unit-triangular polynomial
+coordinate change is a quotient-ring isomorphism, and quotient-ring
+isomorphisms preserve the unit ideal.  Thus the constant residue `64` proves
+emptiness equally in the declared `K2c` basis and in the original
+`C2c/C3c` presentation; a fully expanded inverse would be useful for
+inspection but is not needed to conclude `[1]`.
+
+## Necessity Of Row Families
+
+All row-family claims here are typed as necessary conditions inside the
+declared chart, not as attainment of a Keller map.
+
+`CONFIRMED[COMMON-CHART-ROWS]`.  The chart is the fixed-top triangular tower
+
+```text
+h3 = P + H
+h2 = h3^3 + C2 h3 + C3
+F  = h2^3 + A2 h2 + A3
+G  = h2^2 + B1 h2 + B2
+P  = y^3(y-x)^8.
+```
+
+The label reversal is declared: chart `F` is Moh/Xu `g` of degree 99 and chart
+`G` is Moh/Xu `f` of degree 66.  The minor line at `y=0` and the major line
+at `y=x` are a linear/torus gauge of the two fixed lines, not a degree swap
+and not a numerical slice.
+
+`CONFIRMED[MAJOR-H2-K2C-ROWS]`.  Moh Theorem 1.2 supplies lower-order
+inequalities along the major tower.  Strict-below support entries are
+vanishing rows; equality faces are not rows unless the fixed leading face
+itself supplies the equality.  The common major-h2 structural state has 389
+unit-triangular D2 pivots and seven h2-D1 pivots, leaving the declared 99
+`K2c` directions.
+
+`CONFIRMED[OUTER-D2-D1-ROWS]`.  The outer blocks `A2,A3,B1,B2` are constrained
+by the same Theorem 1.2 inequalities at the first point.  D2 deletes exactly
+5598 strict-below coordinates with thresholds `189,285,93,189`.  Outer D1
+offsets `0..7` contribute raw-row/rank counts
+
+```text
+64/41, 52/38, 40/33, 29/25, 20/19, 11/11, 6/6, 3/3.
+```
+
+The cumulative outer D1 rank is `176`, and stage 8 has no new outer row.  The
+already-deleted D1 labels are recorded as redundant, not as extra rank.
+
+`CONFIRMED[DELTA52-BRANCH-ROWS]`.  The delta-5/2 branch state is
+
+```text
+p = pi(pi^2-c),     c != 0,
+q1 = -2 integral p^3   up to the normalized scaling used in Xu's ODE,
+```
+
+with the Galois-forced `[1,1,1]` cubic split and the charged compatibility
+`b0=0`.  The engine keeps `u,v,c` symbolic and localizes only by `c`; it does
+not set `c=1`.
+
+`CONFIRMED[POLE-ROWS]`.  Direct `F,G` pole rows are coefficients in the
+branch-specific principal-minor Laurent expansion.  For delta-5/2 the
+normalization shifts local powers by `189` for `F` and `126` for `G`.
+Therefore stage-8 local power `16` is the original Laurent exponent
+
+```text
+F: 16 - 189 = -173
+G: 16 - 126 = -110.
+```
+
+The assertion "pole local power 16, `(F,G)=(-173,-110)`" means: impose the
+two raw-support coordinate rows at local power 16 for `F` and the two
+corresponding rows for `G`, namely `coord0` and `coord2`.  These rows are
+forced because an actual polynomial pair in the classified branch cannot
+retain forbidden negative Laurent coefficients beyond the prescribed
+principal-minor face.  Stage 8 kills on one of these necessary rows:
+`stage8_G_local16_coord0`.
+
+`CONFIRMED[JACOBIAN-ROWS]`.  The identity `J(F,G)=1` forces every positive
+homogeneous coefficient of the normalized Jacobian to vanish.  The top
+degree-163 part cancels since `F_99=P^9` and `G_66=P^6`.  The engine imposes
+the charged degree-162 prefix, then stage 0 `k=27`, stage 1 the remaining
+degree-162 coefficients, and for stage `n>=2` every coefficient in total
+degree `163-n`.  Stage 8 therefore imposes all 156 coefficients of degree
+155.  These are necessary rows of `J=1`, not an optional strengthening.
+
+## No Unlicensed Specialization
+
+`CONFIRMED[NO-UNLICENSED-SPECIALIZATION]`.
+
+The gauge `P=y^3(y-x)^8` only fixes the two lines at infinity and their
