+# Hostile gate: delta=5/2 stage-8 kill for the (99,66) joint chart
+
+Date: 2026-09-04 UTC.  Computation artifacts were generated from the
+September 3 lane inputs under `box/g9966d52gate-20260903/`.
+
+## Verdict
+
+`CONFIRMED[DELTA52-STAGE8-DECLARED-NECESSARY-FINITE-CHART-KILL]`.
+
+The charged stage-7 endpoint was replayed mechanically: exact localized
+dimension `869`, outer D2 rank `5598`, outer D1 rank `176`, joint Q-star rank
+`59`, and zero residue.  The pinned stage-8 system was then rerun in the
+foreground with `timeout 3000` and CPU affinity `0,1,2,3`.  It exited `0`;
+the validated stage-8 ledger is `DEAD`.
+
+The seven new Q-star pivots are exactly the Jacobian degree-155 rows
+`k=35..41` on `B1c_7_19..B1c_7_25`, with coefficients
+
+```text
+675, 576, 477, 378, 279, 180, 81.
+```
+
+After all 66 cumulative rational pivots, the only reduced residue is
+
+```text
+stage8_G_local16_coord0 = 64.
+```
+
+Since the coefficient field is `Q`, this gives the explicit membership
+certificate
+
+```text
+1 = (1/64) * stage8_G_local16_coord0.
+```
+
+The raw residue ideal is already `[1]`; localizing at `c != 0` cannot restore
+a point.  An independent characteristic-zero Singular replay of the emitted
+Rabinowitsch script returned dimension `-1`, standard basis `1`, and controls
+`0,1,0`.
+
+Together with the charged delta-2 stage-4 unit row
+`stage4_J_d159_k35 = 6264`, independently replayed here with the same
+Singular controls, both declared split branches are empty inside the declared
+joint chart.
+
+## Custody
+
+The 23 charged inputs in `/tmp/jc2-lane.MvSYEH/inputs` were checked before
+any replay.  The manifest was generated mechanically from
+`xmodel/g9966-delta52-kill-gate-gpt55-20260903.run.v2`, pairing each indexed
+`charged_input_<i>_sha256` with the corresponding
+`charged_input_<i>_basename`; `sha256sum -c` returned `OK` for every input.
+No digest was manually retyped.  The resulting gate manifest is
+`box/g9966d52gate-20260903/charged-inputs.sha256`, SHA-256
+`fad58e40a54625eef336ca634c18568db08769bdfd6872c8ad8c2005954fba63`.
+
+The pinned continuation engine is
+`box/g9966band-20260903/band_engine.py`, SHA-256
+`3bd2937d75d59d59edeca1b89eba286fd2711f2d608109e7fd8971b64e059ac9`.  Its
+transitive frozen view is the earlier Sol input lane
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.cNPqDa/inputs`; the gate driver restored and verified that
+view from `xmodel/g9966-global-band-sol56-20260903.run.v2`, without changing
+the engine.
+
+The stage-7 endpoint custody replay confirmed:
+
+```text
+stage7.json bytes      43433
+stage7.json SHA-256    a85d602dc4599c600c12b04e2c3140f00dafafbb5793b3b05039050cba6159b3
+dimension              869
+residue_count          0
+dimension formula      6702 - 5598 - 176 - 59 = 869
+```
+
+The regenerated stage-8 next-system manifest is byte-identical to the charged
+one:
+
+```text
+next-stage8-system.json SHA-256
+a050af8c5d4bbb703babb2ce2ee57a70c411eb801226ac9f5cdcffbfa0bfa699
+```
+
+It carries the accepted stage-7 path/hash, the 869 unresolved generator names,
+the pinned engine hash, and argv
+
+```text
+python3 box/g9966band-20260903/band_engine.py --branch delta52 --stage 8
+```
+
+The 869-name list was regenerated byte-for-byte as
+`box/g9966d52gate-20260903/stage7-free-coefficients.txt`, SHA-256
+`30d4f3e027d4bb1db62dce3b7226e15f0ac8a74654724d0ede595cc0d10bbbe9`.
+
+## Stage-8 Replay
+
+The foreground run was:
+
+```text
+timeout 3000 bash box/g9966d52gate-20260903/run_stage8.sh
+```
+
+The wrapper checks the pinned engine hash, sets numerical-library thread
+counts to `1`, sets `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`, applies `taskset -c 0,1,2,3`, and runs
+the engine with `--branch delta52 --stage 8 --emit-singular`.  It returned
+
+```text
+stage=8 status=0 cpu_set=0,1,2,3
+```
+
+The promoted and validated result is
+`box/g9966d52gate-20260903/runs/delta52/stage8.json`, SHA-256
+`095c340d7729f97df9a1f1f4709c5afcde00be32fac15cb3ced540e4ae15ccb9`.
+Its expression-level row hash and residue hash match the charged Sol report:
+
+```text
+all_labeled_rows_hash  56dbca47ef766b098f5d65321324f85909a4c9a65d1a1c10079240b41f5c9ec6
+residual_hash          e356693da067de90565ae0275ecd5d6779737e962b9d01476fc46b355ce3ccb4
+```
+
+The whole stage-8 JSON hash differs from the charged Sol JSON because elapsed
+resource fields are run-local.  The mathematical hashes, residue, Singular
+script hash, band specification, and pivot data agree.
+
+Validated stage-8 band:
+
+| item | value |
+|---|---:|
+| outer D1 offset | none |
+| pole local power | 16 |
+| F pole exponent | -173 |
+| G pole exponent | -110 |
+| Jacobian t-power | 8 |
+| Jacobian total degree | 155 |
+| Jacobian rows | 156, `k=0..155` |
+| F pole rows | 2, `coord0`, `coord2` |
+| G pole rows | 2, `coord0`, `coord2` |
+| external wall / RSS | `1870.89 s / 279056 KiB` |
+
+The new row family is therefore exactly 160 rows: four pole rows and the full
+degree-155 Jacobian row family.  There is no stage-8 outer-D1 row, because
+the outer D1 boundary was exhausted at offset 7 and cumulative rank 176.
+
+The stage history is
+
+```text
+1063 -> 1016 -> 974 -> 940 -> 913 -> 894 -> 880 -> 869 -> DEAD.
+```
+
+The run stopped by unit ideal, not by the two-band stagnation rule, a small
+nonempty dimension, or a budget stop.
+
+## Pivots And Residue
+
+The seven new pivots, all in `Q*`, are:
+
+| row | pivot | coefficient |
+|---|---|---:|
+| `stage8_J_d155_k35` | `B1c_7_19` | 675 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k36` | `B1c_7_20` | 576 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k37` | `B1c_7_21` | 477 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k38` | `B1c_7_22` | 378 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k39` | `B1c_7_23` | 279 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k40` | `B1c_7_24` | 180 |
+| `stage8_J_d155_k41` | `B1c_7_25` | 81 |
+
+The localization parameter `c` is never eligible for Q-star elimination:
+the engine reduces with `set(all_free)-{c}` and asserts that `c` remains.
+Every cumulative pivot coefficient parses as a nonzero rational.  There are
+no retired pivots.
+
+Before the residue, the formal remaining-generator count is `862`.  This is
+not a surviving family dimension.  The single residual row is the exact normal
+form
+
+```text
+stage8_G_local16_coord0 = 64.
+```
+
+The emitted Singular script is
+`box/g9966d52gate-20260903/runs/delta52/stage8.sing`, SHA-256
+`36f7f21f9faa3f7fec6b1d9353a194c17c6aecb8d2a5c2e48096b680c6e77b2e`.  It is
+the characteristic-zero ring `Q[c,Zc]` with ideal `64, Zc*c-1`, plus the
+three controls.  The independent replay output has SHA-256
+`236517b4a8e5567c586d39194059d49207001416a1d922efaec1fc3d2b9c7b73` and
+prints:
+
+```text
+BEGIN_DIM
+-1
+END_DIM
+BEGIN_GB
+1
+END_GB
+BEGIN_CONTROLS
+0
+1
+0
+END_CONTROLS
+```
+
+The controls mean: the deliberately empty localization is unit, the point
+localization is nonunit, and the raw constant residue ideal is unit.
+
+## K2c Coordinate Change
+
+The stage engine computes in the declared `K2c` basis:
+
+```text
+K2c_r_q = [t^r(w-1)^q](K3^3 + (t^22 C2)K3 + t^33 C3),
+```
+
+for low `q`, after the major h2 D2 structural state.  The charged structural
+certificate states that the unit leader is `C3c_r_q` for `q<=10` and
+`C2c_r_(q-11)` for `11<=q<=21`.
+
+This gate reconstructs and serializes the inverse as a compact triangular
+ledger:
+
+```text
+box/g9966d52gate-20260903/k2c-c2c3-inverse.json
+SHA-256 88e717d691f6ab35336e3a0a387463f4c319d5917c37c417a54f8a2dddf9a768
+```
+
+The ledger has 495 inverse rules, one for each original low-q `C2c/C3c`
+coordinate:
+
+```text
+C2c variables                         187
+C3c variables                         308
+low-q nonidentity output slots         495
+D2 fixed low-q slots                   389
+D2 identity slots outside low-q        (1,22), (1,23), (2,22)
+K2c coordinates before h2-D1           106
+K2c coordinates after h2-D1             99
+inverse_rules_sha256
+aabd8ce03875fcab6432b27f0af8151a2e796ff717d646b8c66af4cb58f37495
+```
+
+The inverse is compact, not fully expanded.  Each rule has diagonal
+coefficient `1` and every nonleader `C2c` dependency is solved earlier in the
+`(r,-q)` order.  The seven h2-D1 eliminations are also recorded:
+
+```text
+K2c_11_16, K2c_15_13, K2c_19_10, K2c_23_7, K2c_27_4,
+K2c_10_17, K2c_14_14
+```
+
+with coefficients
+
+```text
+1, -3, 9, -27, 81, 1, -3.
+```
+
+This is enough for the stage-8 conclusion.  A unit-triangular polynomial
+coordinate change is a quotient-ring isomorphism, and quotient-ring
+isomorphisms preserve the unit ideal.  Thus the constant residue `64` proves
+emptiness equally in the declared `K2c` basis and in the original
+`C2c/C3c` presentation; a fully expanded inverse would be useful for
+inspection but is not needed to conclude `[1]`.
+
+## Necessity Of Row Families
+
+All row-family claims here are typed as necessary conditions inside the
+declared chart, not as attainment of a Keller map.
+
+`CONFIRMED[COMMON-CHART-ROWS]`.  The chart is the fixed-top triangular tower
+
+```text
+h3 = P + H
+h2 = h3^3 + C2 h3 + C3
+F  = h2^3 + A2 h2 + A3
+G  = h2^2 + B1 h2 + B2
+P  = y^3(y-x)^8.
+```
+
